From b807173e04db1dd1ffb48ae944cd27b10cd48cdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@buttzeppelin>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 12:47:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Per-stat inflection points and boss classification
 overrides (F-207)

Per-stat inflection points
--------------------------
Upstream applies a single inflection point to health, mana, armor, damage and
CC duration alike, so it cannot express "damage falls off faster than health at
low player counts". The flat StatModifier* settings that can do this are applied
across the whole curve, so they also weaken a full group.

Adds AutoBalance.InflectionPoint<Type>.PerStat, one per instance type, in the
format "[Health] [Mana] [Armor] [Damage] [CCDuration]" where -1 or an omitted
value leaves that stat on the standard inflection point. Values use the same
units as the base InflectionPoint* setting, and CurveFloor, CurveCeiling and
BossModifier still apply, so an overridden stat still converges to full strength
at max players.

getStatDefaultMultiplier() returns the caller's already-computed multiplier
unchanged when a stat has no override, so the default path is untouched.

Boss classification overrides
-----------------------------
The core derives CREATURE_FLAG_EXTRA_DUNGEON_BOSS solely from instance_encounters
rows whose encounter id exists in DungeonEncounter.dbc, and strips the flag if it
is set in the database. Bosses Blizzard never gave a DungeonEncounter row are
therefore scaled as trash.

Adds AutoBalance.ForceBossID and AutoBalance.ForceTrashID. ForceTrashID wins and
short-circuits summon inheritance, so demoting a creature demotes its summons.
isBossOrBossSummon() now delegates to a shared isBossCreature() for both the
creature and its summoner, so the two paths cannot disagree.

.ab creaturestat reports "| Boss (forced)" / "| Trash (forced)".

